draft.language:
8.1 Start2 shall not disclose any business information or materials of Company ("Company Confidential Information") obtained under this Agreement to any third party without Company's prior written consent, and shall protect it with at least the same degree of care it uses for its own confidential information.

8.2 Company shall not disclose any lecture materials, business information, business know-how, methodology, processes, techniques, records, or other business, technical, or financial information of Start2 ("Start2 Confidential Information", together with Company Confidential Information, "Confidential Information") obtained under this Agreement to any third party without Start2's prior written consent, and shall protect it with the same degree of care.

8.3 This obligation does not apply to Confidential Information that:
(a) is provided by Company's startups for evaluation by potential clients, experts, or mentors, or for any other purpose necessary in connection with the Service;
(b) is or becomes publicly available other than by breach of this Agreement;
(c) was already known to the receiving Party before disclosure;
(d) is independently developed without reference to the disclosing Party's Confidential Information;
(e) the disclosing Party has consented in writing to disclose; or
(f) is received from a third party not known to be under a confidentiality obligation to the disclosing Party.

8.4 This Clause survives termination or expiry of this Agreement.

must_have.reference_clause:
Any notices, communications, demands, requests, approvals, or consents shall be deemed to be duly given and received:
11.2.1 if personally delivered, on the day of delivery;
11.2.2 if sent by pre-paid registered mail from an address in one country to an address also in the same country, two (2) days after the same is sent;
11.2.3 if sent by pre-paid registered mail from an address in one country to an address in another country, seven (7) days after the same is sent;
11.2.4 if sent by facsimile, upon the issue of report of confirmation of successful transmission by the machine used by the sender to send the facsimile, subject to a confirmation copy being sent by post within forty-eight (48) hours; and
11.2.5 if sent by email, at the time of transmission, provided that the sender does not receive any automated message indicting failed delivery or non-receipt.

Either party may from time to time by written notice to the other designate a different address applicable or designate a different person to whose attention the notices, communications, demands, requests, approvals, or consents must be addressed.

