13.1 Either Party ("Non-Defaulting Party") may terminate this Agreement immediately on written notice to the other Party ("Defaulting Party") if:
(a) the Defaulting Party commits a material breach of this Agreement and fails to remedy it within 14 days of written notice requiring remedy;
(b) the Defaulting Party becomes insolvent, has a receiver or liquidator appointed, or is unable to pay its debts;
(c) the Defaulting Party assigns its rights under this Agreement without consent; or
(d) the Defaulting Party acts in a manner that seriously damages the Non-Defaulting Party's reputation or business.
13.2 On early termination, Start2 is entitled to payment for the Service Fee for work performed up to the date of termination, in addition to its rights under Clause [Cost Recovery on Cancellation].

